- How would you adapt for at-most-k windows instead of exactly k?
- How would you reconstruct the actual windows efficiently and handle negative values?

## Why This Is Asked
Tests DP formulation for selecting multiple non-overlapping subarrays, a common beginner challenge with practical reconstruction.

## Key Concepts
- dp[i][t]: best sum using first i elements with exactly t subarrays
- end[i][t]: best subarray sum ending at i-1 for t subarrays
- Transitions combine extending a subarray or starting a new one
- Reconstruction via backtracking boundaries

## Code Example
```javascript
function maxKSubarrays(A, k) {
  const n = A.length;
  const NEG = -Infinity;
  const dp = Array.from({length: n+1}, () => Array(k+1).fill(NEG));
  const end = Array.from({length: n+1}, () => Array(k+1).fill(NEG));
  for (let i = 0; i <= n; i++) dp[i][0] = 0;
  for (let i = 1; i <= n; i++) {
    for (let t = 1; t <= k; t++) {
      end[i][t] = Math.max(end[i-1][t] + A[i-1], dp[i-1][t-1] + A[i-1]);
      dp[i][t] = Math.max(dp[i-1][t], end[i][t]);
    }
  }
  return {best: dp[n][k]};
}
```

## Follow-up Questions
- How would you adapt for at-most-k subarrays?
- How would you retrieve the actual subarray boundaries efficiently?

## Why This Is Asked
This problem extends the classic Longest Palindromic Subsequence (LPS) problem by allowing up to k character deletions, requiring a 3D DP formulation. It tests understanding of subsequence DP with additional constraints, careful boundary handling, and the ability to reconstruct the solution path.

## Key Concepts
- Longest Palindromic Subsequence with deletions
- 3D DP (i, j, d) where d represents remaining deletions
- Path reconstruction for deletion decisions
- Time/space complexity: O(n²·k) time, O(n²·k) space

## Code Example
```javascript
function longestPalindromicSubseqWithDeletions(s, k) {
  const n = s.length;
  const dp = Array.from({ length: n }, () =>
    Array.from({ length: n }, () => Array(k + 1).fill(0))
  );

  for (let i = 0; i < n; i++) {
    for (let d = 0; d <= k; d++) {
      dp[i][i][d] = 1;
    }
  }

  for (let len = 2; len <= n; len++) {
    for (let i = 0; i + len <= n; i++) {
      const j = i + len - 1;
      for (let d = 0; d <= k; d++) {
        if (s[i] === s[j]) {
          dp[i][j][d] = Math.max(dp[i][j][d], (len > 2 ? dp[i + 1][j - 1][d] : 0) + 2);
        }
        if (d > 0) {
          dp[i][j][d] = Math.max(dp[i][j][d], dp[i + 1][j][d - 1], dp[i][j - 1][d - 1]);
        }
      }
    }
  }

  return dp[0][n - 1][k];
}
```

## Why This Is Asked
This tests minimax-style DP with reconstruction for a classic game.

## Key Concepts
- Two-player DP with difference state
- Subarray DP and reconstruction path
- Time: O(n^2) space: O(n^2)

## Code Example
```javascript
// dp[i][j] denotes max diff for i..j
function maxFirstPlayer(values){
  const n = values.length; const dp = Array.from({length:n},()=>Array(n).fill(0));
  let total = values.reduce((a,b)=>a+b,0);
  for(let i=0;i<n;i++) dp[i][i]=values[i];
  for(let len=2; len<=n; len++){
    for(let i=0;i+len-1<n;i++){
      const j=i+len-1;
      dp[i][j] = Math.max(values[i]-dp[i+1][j], values[j]-dp[i][j-1]);
    }
  }
  return (total + dp[0][n-1])/2;
}
```

## Follow-up Questions
- How would you reconstruct the exact L/R sequence from the DP table?
- How does this change if moves include taking from both ends with a coin flip to decide who starts?

## Why This Is Asked
This tests DP partitioning with a non-trivial per-segment cost that depends on both sum and min, plus reconstruction.

## Key Concepts
- Partition DP with exact k segments
- Precompute minVal(l,r) in O(n^2)
- Transition uses prefix sums and minVal; reconstruct with parent pointers

## Code Example
```javascript
function maxCost(A, k){
  const n = A.length;
  const pref = new Array(n+1).fill(0);
  for(let i=1;i<=n;i++) pref[i] = pref[i-1] + A[i-1];
  // minVal[l][r]
  const minVal = Array.from({length:n+2}, ()=>Array(n+2).fill(0));
  for(let l=1;l<=n;l++){
    let m = A[l-1];
    minVal[l][l] = m;
    for(let r=l;r<=n;r++){
      m = (r===l) ? A[l-1] : Math.min(m, A[r-1]);
      minVal[l][r] = m;
    }
  }
  const dp = Array.from({length:n+1}, ()=>Array(k+1).fill(-Infinity));
  const par = Array.from({length:n+1}, ()=>Array(k+1).fill(-1));
  for(let i=1;i<=n;i++){ dp[i][1] = (pref[i]-pref[0]) * minVal[1][i]; par[i][1] = 0; }
  for(let t=2;t<=k;t++){
    for(let i=t;i<=n;i++){
      for(let p=t-1;p<=i-1;p++){
        const val = dp[p][t-1] + (pref[i]-pref[p]) * minVal[p+1][i];
        if(val > dp[i][t]){ dp[i][t] = val; par[i][t] = p; }
      }
    }
  }
  // reconstruction omitted for brevity
  return {best: dp[n][k]};
}
```
